{# ── A LONG ADMIN FORM, MADE FILLABLE ─────────────────────────────────────────

   Included by the event and product editors. It is styles and one Alpine component, no
   markup of its own, so each form keeps its own fields and only borrows the structure.

   ══ THE PROBLEM IT SOLVES ══════════════════════════════════════════════════

   The event editor is 49 inputs and the product editor 25, each in a single undifferentiated
   column with repeaters buried in the middle and one Save button at the very bottom. Measured,
   not guessed. That shape fails in four specific ways, and all four were reported as "confusing":

     • THERE IS NO SENSE OF WHAT IS REQUIRED. Title and slug are mandatory; twenty-nine other
       fields are not. Nothing on screen said so, so the honest way to create an event was to
       read all forty and decide for yourself.
     • THERE IS NO SENSE OF WHERE YOU ARE. Somebody who has typed the name and the price cannot
       tell whether they are nearly done or a third of the way, so they keep scrolling to check.
     • THE ORDER IS THE DATABASE'S, NOT THE JOB'S. Cover image sits between capacity and status
       because that is the column order, and "what am I selling" is interleaved with "how does it
       sell" and "what happens after".
     • AND SAVE IS AT THE BOTTOM OF A LONG SCROLL, so correcting one field means finding it,
       changing it, then scrolling past everything else to commit it.

   ══ WHY STEPS AND NOT PAGES ════════════════════════════════════════════════

   Splitting into separate pages would mean separate saves, and a half-created event in the
   database is worse than a long form: the tier repeater, the agenda and the ticket design all
   write in one transaction from one POST, and the existing controllers read marker fields to
   know which sections were on screen. Breaking that would risk silently dropping somebody's
   work — which is the failure mode this whole codebase keeps finding.

   So EVERY FIELD STAYS IN ONE FORM AND IN THE DOM. The steps only change what is VISIBLE. One
   Save still posts everything, the controllers are untouched, and nothing can be lost by
   navigating between steps because navigating does not submit anything.

   ══ AND IT WORKS WITHOUT JAVASCRIPT ════════════════════════════════════════

   `.af` starts with every step visible; the component adds `is-live` on boot and only then does
   the CSS hide the inactive ones. If Alpine never loads, an admin gets exactly the long form
   they have today — which is worse than the stepped version and infinitely better than a page
   with one visible field and no way to reach the rest. #}

<style nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}">
  .af{ display:block }

  /* ── the rail ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Numbered, named, and carrying a count of what is still required — so "where am I" and
     "what is left" are answered without scrolling. On a phone it becomes a horizontal strip,
     because a vertical rail would take the whole screen before the form began. */
  .af__rail{ display:flex; gap:8px; overflow-x:auto; scrollbar-width:none;
    padding:2px 0 14px; margin-bottom:4px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--ad-line,#e2e8e6) }
  .af__rail::-webkit-scrollbar{ display:none }
  .af__tab{ flex:none; cursor:pointer; display:flex; align-items:center; gap:9px;
    border:1px solid var(--ad-line,#e2e8e6); background:var(--ad-surface,#fff);
    border-radius:999px; padding:8px 15px 8px 10px; font-family:inherit; font-size:13px;
    font-weight:600; color:var(--ad-text-mute,#5a6d6f) }
  .af__tab:hover{ border-color:rgba(16,41,44,.28); color:var(--ad-text,#10292C) }
  .af__tab.is-on{ background:#10292C; border-color:#10292C; color:#fff }
  .af__n{ flex:none; width:21px; height:21px; border-radius:50%; display:flex;
    align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-size:11px; font-weight:700;
    background:#eef2f1; color:#5a6d6f }
  .af__tab.is-on .af__n{ background:rgba(255,255,255,.2); color:#fff }
  /* A count of REQUIRED fields still empty on that step. Not a validity tick: a green tick on
     a step whose optional fields are untouched would say "done" about something nobody has
     looked at, and that is a worse lie than saying nothing. */
  .af__todo{ flex:none; min-width:18px; height:18px; padding:0 5px; border-radius:999px;
    display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-size:10.5px; font-weight:700;
    background:#fdeaea; color:#a4243a }
  .af__tab.is-on .af__todo{ background:#fff; color:#a4243a }
  .af__done{ flex:none; width:16px; height:16px; color:#1a6118 }
  .af__tab.is-on .af__done{ color:#7FC87C }

  /* ── the steps ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Every step is in the DOM always; only display changes, and only once the component has
     booted (`.af.is-live`). Without script every step stays visible — see the note above. */
  .af.is-live .af__step{ display:none }
  .af.is-live .af__step.is-on{ display:block }
  .af__step{ animation:afIn .16s ease-out }
  @keyframes afIn{ from{ opacity:0; transform:translateY(3px) } to{ opacity:1; transform:none } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce){ .af__step{ animation:none } }

  .af__head{ margin:4px 0 14px }
  .af__head h2{ margin:0; font-size:17px; font-weight:700; color:var(--ad-text,#10292C) }
  .af__head p{ margin:5px 0 0; font-size:13px; line-height:1.6; color:var(--ad-text-mute,#5a6d6f) }

  /* Required fields marked, once, consistently. The absence of this was most of the confusion:
     an admin cannot tell a mandatory field from an optional one by looking at it. */
  .af-req{ color:#a4243a; font-weight:700; margin-left:2px }
  .af-opt{ font-weight:400; color:var(--ad-text-mute,#8a9a9c); font-size:11.5px; margin-left:4px }

  /* ── the bar ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Sticky, so Save is never a scroll away, and it SAYS whether there is anything unsaved.
     A Save button that looks identical whether or not you have changed something is a button
     you press again just in case. */
  .af__bar{ position:sticky; bottom:0; z-index:5; display:flex; align-items:center; gap:12px;
    flex-wrap:wrap; margin-top:18px; padding:13px 0;
    background:linear-gradient(to top, var(--ad-bg,#f4f7f4) 62%, rgba(244,247,244,0));
    border-top:1px solid var(--ad-line,#e2e8e6);
    /* Room for the assistant button, which is `position:fixed` at right:20px / bottom:20px on
       every admin page (admin/partials/copilot.twig). Without this it sits directly on top of
       Save — seen in a screenshot, with the word "changes" disappearing under it. A sticky bar
       and a fixed button both anchored to the bottom-right WILL collide; the bar is the one
       that can move. */
    padding-right:88px }
  .af__state{ flex:1; min-width:150px; font-size:12.5px; color:var(--ad-text-mute,#5a6d6f) }
  .af__state.is-dirty{ color:#8a5a00; font-weight:600 }
  .af__state.is-blocked{ color:#a4243a; font-weight:600 }
  .af__steps{ display:flex; gap:8px }
  .af__ghost{ cursor:pointer; border:1px solid var(--ad-line,#e2e8e6);
    background:var(--ad-surface,#fff); color:var(--ad-text,#10292C); font-family:inherit;
    font-size:13px; font-weight:600; padding:10px 16px; border-radius:999px }
  .af__ghost:disabled{ opacity:.4; cursor:not-allowed }

  @media (max-width:620px){
    .af__bar{ padding:11px 0 }
    .af__state{ order:3; flex-basis:100% }
    .af__steps{ flex:1 }
    .af__ghost{ flex:1; text-align:center }
  }
</style>

<script nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}">
/* ── afSteps ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   `titles` names the steps. Everything else is read from the DOM rather than declared twice:
   the component counts its own `.af__step` children and finds required fields inside them, so
   adding a field to a form never means editing a parallel list here. A parallel list is how a
   step ends up claiming a field it does not contain.

   NOTHING HERE VALIDATES. The browser already does it with `required`, and the server does it
   properly. This only COUNTS what the browser reports, so the rail can say "2 left" — a second
   opinion about validity is a second thing to disagree with the first. */
function afSteps(titles){
  return {
    titles: titles || [],
    at: 0,
    dirty: false,
    /* Recomputed on input rather than watched per field: one listener on the form beats one
       per input, and there are forty of them. */
    todo: [],

    init(){
      /* `is-live` is what lets the CSS hide anything. Added HERE, so a page whose script never
         ran shows every step — the long form, which is what an admin has today, rather than a
         page with one section and no way to reach the others. */
      this.$el.classList.add('is-live');
      this.count();

      /* Reopen on the step somebody was on, per form, so a save that bounces back — or a
         mis-click — does not throw them to the beginning of a forty-field form. sessionStorage
         rather than a cookie: it is per tab and it expires by itself. */
      try{
        var k = this.key();
        var was = parseInt(sessionStorage.getItem(k) || '0', 10);
        if(!isNaN(was) && was > 0 && was < this.titles.length) this.at = was;
      }catch(e){}

      /* One delegated listener for the whole form. `input` for typing, `change` for selects and
         checkboxes — a select fires only `change`, and without it the rail's count goes stale
         the moment somebody picks a category. */
      var self = this;
      ['input','change'].forEach(function(ev){
        self.$el.addEventListener(ev, function(){ self.dirty = true; self.count(); });
      });

      /* Leaving with unsaved work is the one thing worth interrupting for. Only when dirty, and
         removed on submit so saving never triggers it. */
      window.addEventListener('beforeunload', function(e){
        if(!self.dirty) return;
        e.preventDefault(); e.returnValue = '';
      });
      var form = this.$el.closest('form') || this.$el.querySelector('form');
      if(form) form.addEventListener('submit', function(){ self.dirty = false; });
    },

    key(){ return 'afStep:' + (location.pathname || 'form'); },

    steps(){ return Array.from(this.$el.querySelectorAll('.af__step')); },

    /* How many REQUIRED fields are still empty, per step. Uses the browser's own view of
       validity, so a pattern or a type the markup declares is honoured without restating it. */
    count(){
      this.todo = this.steps().map(function(step){
        var need = step.querySelectorAll('[required]');
        var n = 0;
        for(var i = 0; i < need.length; i++){
          var el = need[i];
          if(el.disabled) continue;
          /* offsetParent is null for a field inside a collapsed section — a step that is not
             showing still counts, because its fields are real; but a field hidden by its own
             form logic (an axis nobody chose) is not something to demand. */
          if(el.type !== 'hidden' && el.closest('[hidden]')) continue;
          if(!el.checkValidity()) n++;
        }
        return n;
      });
    },

    go(i){
      if(i < 0 || i >= this.titles.length) return;
      this.at = i;
      try{ sessionStorage.setItem(this.key(), String(i)); }catch(e){}
      /* Back to the top of the step, because arriving halfway down a section reads as a broken
         page. `instant` rather than smooth: this is a jump, not a journey. */
      var top = this.$el.getBoundingClientRect().top + window.scrollY - 90;
      window.scrollTo({ top: top > 0 ? top : 0, behavior: 'instant' });
    },
    next(){ this.go(this.at + 1); },
    back(){ this.go(this.at - 1); },
    isOn(i){ return this.at === i; },

    /* The total still outstanding, for the bar. */
    left(){ return this.todo.reduce(function(a, b){ return a + b; }, 0); },

    /* What the bar says. Three states, because they mean different things: nothing to do,
       something to save, and something missing that will stop the save being accepted. */
    state(){
      var n = this.left();
      if(n > 0) return n === 1 ? '1 required field still empty' : n + ' required fields still empty';
      if(this.dirty) return 'Unsaved changes';
      return 'Everything saved';
    },
    stateClass(){
      if(this.left() > 0) return 'is-blocked';
      return this.dirty ? 'is-dirty' : '';
    }
  };
}
</script>
